/*
  core/masks/outcome_degraded_click.spthy -- OPT-IN outcome rows: a DEGRADED user still fires the
  primary-goal click (an extension of the outcome matrix, like outcome_habituated_clickthrough).

  The default matrix gives 'authorize' only Attentive->grant and Fearful->abort: under any other
  active degrade the step stalls. That is the right default for a SECURITY authorization (P3's
  authorize phase). But the final "send" button of a composer is the PRIMARY-GOAL action, not a
  security check: degraded-but-engaged users still complete the task they came to do -- attentional
  degradation hits the CHECKS along the way, not the goal click (Reason's GEMS: slips and lapses
  strike the checking/monitoring steps; the intention to send survives). Only Fearful (frozen past
  the Yerkes-Dodson peak) refuses, and Attentive grants as before.

    Busy / Habituated / Naive / Careless + authorize -> grant

  Opt-in, NOT global, so profiles whose 'authorize' models a security gate keep the stall default.
  Include alongside outcome_policy (S3 does). Persistent + read-only, seeded unconditionally ->
  closed theory, no sources loop; OnceDegradedClick bounds the seed.
*/

rule Seed_degraded_click [color=#9b51e0]:
    [ ]
  --[ SeedDegradedClick() ]->
    [ !OutcomePolicy('Busy',      'authorize', 'grant'),
      !OutcomePolicy('Habituated','authorize', 'grant'),
      !OutcomePolicy('Naive',     'authorize', 'grant'),
      !OutcomePolicy('Careless',  'authorize', 'grant') ]

restriction OnceDegradedClick:
  "All #i #j. SeedDegradedClick()@i & SeedDegradedClick()@j ==> #i = #j"
